The reviewed stack is read-only/non-live in the scoped paths and the targeted unit suites pass, but the stream-growth calculation fails the non-empty stalled-stream case required for zero-growth liveness detection.

Review comment:

- [P1] Treat repeated latest stream IDs as no growth — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/growth_calculator.py:40-44
  When the stream already has an entry and then stops growing, `latest_stream_id()` will keep returning the same Redis ID on every poll; this code counts that repeated ID as one unit of `prediction_stream_id_growth`, so `evaluate_liveness()` never reaches its `prediction_stream_id_growth == 0` alert path for a non-empty stalled stream. That misses the required zero-growth liveness condition until another SLA happens to trip, so the growth calculation needs to represent actual ID advancement rather than distinct IDs observed.
